      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1700 mg PO per day**, either divided (for example 850 mg twice daily) or as a once-daily total\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you've confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me which of the corrected doses to use."
      }
